The purpose of the project was to design and implement a decentralized hotel booking system using blockchain  technology and Ethereum smart contracts.
Traditional hotel booking platforms rely on centralized databases and third-party payment providers to manage reservation and process payments while effective
, these systems can introduce transaction fees delay, and trust issues between customers and service providers. Blockchain technology offers an alternative by
providing a transparent, immutable service decentralized ledger where transactions can be verified without relying on intermediaries (Ethereum Foundation 2024).

This project developed a HotelBooking smart contract using Solidity and deployed it on a local Ethereum blockchain using Ganache. The solution uses a secure escrow
mechanism that stores guest payments within the smart contract until the guest successfully checks into the hotel. This approach increases trust between both parties while
demonstrating the practical application of blockchain technologies in the hospitality industry.
